            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0707" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1599: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-13T16:00:00+08:00">February 13, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—7:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 10, 1 p.m., to Nanking. Formal proposal has been received. My
                    British colleague recommended to his Government favorable consideration in
                    principle.</p>
                <p>I believe we should not object but we must of course bear in mind that the
                    Chinese may never resume payments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
